Z||000000||Sootah||09-08-2001||08:55 PM||||I am looking at a 1988 Coupe, so far my only beef w/ it is that it has an auto tranny. How hard are these to swap? Can I do it myself (I r dumbass when it comes to cars) or how much would it cost me to have done for me? Also, would I need a new ECM?<P>Thanx<BR>-<B>Sootah</B><BR><P>------------------<BR><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I>||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||09-08-2001||09:23 PM||||You might ought to drive it before you decide that. Becuase of how a torque converter works, the 4 cylinder delivers allot more torque into the tranny than you think. The TC lockup feature means the autogets allot better fuel economy than people think as well.<P>It can be done but it's a major project.<BR>you have to setup all the clutch stuff. change the tranny, shifter system, and axles. change the ECM PROM.<P>If that sounds easy,,, read all the threads on Fiero clutch problems. Even with all new clutch parts people have problems.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sootah||09-08-2001||09:29 PM||||Yeah, I figured it'd end up being a massive pain in the ass. I think I will offer the guy $500 for it and let him talk me up to $600. If not, then I will get the SE.<P>Also, how much would a decent paint job run me? Not showroom or anything, but I may want to sell the coupe if I find a better one and it sounds like it could use a touch-up job. Maaco do a decent job?||||reg||1
